nrc-nuclear pack: content licence
=================================

This pack is derived from the seven US Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC)
sources listed below (S1 to S7 of the source-vetting record). Their landing-page
URLs are held in the local source manifest dated 2026-09-26 and are not
reproduced here; the repository link policy bans source-material hosts (see
../../docs/LICENSING.md).

Source licence: Public Domain (US Government work, 17 U.S.C. 105)  (tier 1; see
../../docs/SOURCE-VETTING.md). No source-material download link is published.

All seven sources are works of the United States Government prepared by NRC
staff, and are NOT subject to copyright protection in the United States
(17 U.S.C. 105). They are in the public domain: anyone may reproduce, transform,
and redistribute them for any purpose, including commercially, without
permission and without any attribution or share-alike obligation.

Attribution to the NRC is provided as a courtesy (see the repository NOTICE),
not as a legal obligation. The NRC does not endorse this pack or its authors.

Each source below carries a vetting block: exact title, revision and date, ML
accession, licence basis, what the pack reconstructs from it, and the chapters
that use it. Titles and section structures were checked against the local
source-text captures on 2026-09-26.

Reconstruction: all pack content is synthesized reference notes in the authors'
own words. The documents themselves are not republished here; quotations are
limited to short passages (two-sentence cap per quote, enforced by the pack
gates).

NOTE: This file governs the CONTENT of this pack. The repository tooling is
licensed separately under MIT (see ../../LICENSE).


THE SEVEN SOURCES
=================

S1  Regulatory Guide 1.168, "Verification, Validation, Reviews, and Audits for
    Digital Computer Software Used in Safety Systems of Nuclear Power Plants"
    Publisher: US Nuclear Regulatory Commission
    Revision 2   Issued: July 2013   ML accession: ML13073A210
    Licence: Public Domain (US Government work)
    Reconstructs: the guide's purpose and discussion background, and the staff
    regulatory guidance on verification and validation of digital computer
    software used in safety systems: software integrity, software reliability,
    independence of software verification and validation, conformance of
    materials, quality assurance, tools for software development, verification
    and validation tasks, and reviews and audits.
    Used in: ch01, ch05

S2  Regulatory Guide 1.169, "Configuration Management Plans for Digital Computer
    Software Used in Safety Systems of Nuclear Power Plants"
    Publisher: US Nuclear Regulatory Commission
    Revision 1   Issued: July 2013   ML accession: ML12355A642
    Licence: Public Domain (US Government work)
    Reconstructs: the guide's purpose and discussion background, and the staff
    regulatory guidance on the content of a software configuration management
    plan: configuration identification, configuration control, interface
    control, and configuration status accounting for safety-system software.
    Used in: ch01, ch04

S3  Regulatory Guide 1.170, "Test Documentation for Digital Computer Software
    Used in Safety Systems of Nuclear Power Plants"
    Publisher: US Nuclear Regulatory Commission
    Revision 1   Issued: July 2013   ML accession: ML13003A216
    Licence: Public Domain (US Government work)
    Reconstructs: the guide's purpose and discussion background, and the staff
    regulatory guidance on software test documentation: the test plan, test
    design specification, test case specification, test procedure, and test
    results and reports for safety-system software.
    Used in: ch01, ch06

S4  Regulatory Guide 1.171, "Software Unit Testing for Digital Computer Software
    Used in Safety Systems of Nuclear Power Plants"
    Publisher: US Nuclear Regulatory Commission
    Revision 1   Issued: July 2013   ML accession: ML13004A375
    Licence: Public Domain (US Government work)
    Reconstructs: the guide's purpose and discussion background, and the staff
    regulatory guidance on unit testing of safety-system software: unit test
    planning, test case design and coverage, test execution and recording, and
    evaluation of unit test results.
    Used in: ch01, ch06

S5  Regulatory Guide 1.172, "Software Requirement Specifications for Digital
    Computer Software and Complex Electronics Used in Safety Systems of Nuclear
    Power Plants"
    Publisher: US Nuclear Regulatory Commission
    Revision 1   Issued: July 2013   ML accession: ML13007A173
    Licence: Public Domain (US Government work)
    Reconstructs: the guide's purpose and discussion background, and the staff
    regulatory guidance on the content of a software requirements
    specification for safety-system software and complex electronics:
    functional and performance requirements, design constraints, and the
    qualities of a good requirements specification.
    Used in: ch01, ch03

S6  Regulatory Guide 1.173, "Developing Software Life-Cycle Processes for
    Digital Computer Software Used in Safety Systems of Nuclear Power Plants"
    Publisher: US Nuclear Regulatory Commission
    Revision 1   Issued: July 2013   ML accession: ML13009A190
    Licence: Public Domain (US Government work)
    Reconstructs: the guide's purpose and discussion background, and the staff
    regulatory guidance on developing software life cycle processes: process
    definition and integration, development, verification and validation,
    configuration management, and the software plans that document them.
    Used in: ch01, ch02

S7  NUREG-0800 Standard Review Plan, Branch Technical Position 7-14, "Guidance
    on Software Reviews for Digital Computer-Based Instrumentation and Control
    Systems"
    Publisher: US Nuclear Regulatory Commission
    Revision 6   Issued: August 2016   ML accession: ML16019A308
    Licence: Public Domain (US Government work)
    Reconstructs: the staff's software review positions: the background and
    review of the description of the software aspects of the application;
    the information to be reviewed; the acceptance criteria for planning
    (the software management, development, quality assurance, integration,
    installation, maintenance, training, operations, and safety plans, plus
    the verification and validation, configuration management, and test plan
    reviews); the acceptance criteria for implementation; the acceptance
    criteria for design outputs (the requirements, architecture, and design
    outputs, and the implementation, integration, and installation outputs);
    and the review procedures.
    Used in: ch01, ch02, ch04, ch05, ch06, ch07


EXCLUDED MATERIAL (cited by designation and edition only; no text reproduced)
=============================================================================

The following standards and guides are endorsed, referenced, or adjacent to the
seven sources. They are NOT licensed to this pack: the NRC documents name them,
and the pack restates only the NRC's own recognition and discussion text. It
reproduces no standard text, table, requirement, or clause wording from any of
them.

-   X1  IEEE Std 603-1991, criteria for safety systems for nuclear power
        generating stations. Copyrighted; cited by designation and edition only.
-   X2  IEEE Std 7-4.3.2-2003, criteria for programmable digital devices in
        safety systems. Copyrighted; cited by designation and edition only.
-   X3  IEEE Std 828-2005, configuration management in systems and software.
        Copyrighted; cited by designation and edition only.
-   X4  IEEE Std 829-2008, software test documentation. Copyrighted; cited by
        designation and edition only.
-   X5  IEEE Std 830-1998, recommended practice for software requirements
        specifications. Copyrighted; cited by designation and edition only.
-   X6  IEEE Std 1008-1987, software unit testing. Copyrighted; cited by
        designation and edition only.
-   X7  IEEE Std 1012-2004, software verification and validation. Copyrighted;
        cited by designation and edition only.
-   X8  IEEE Std 1028-2008, software reviews and audits. Copyrighted; cited by
        designation and edition only.
-   X9  IEEE Std 1074-2006, developing software life cycle processes.
        Copyrighted; cited by designation and edition only.
-   X10 IEC 60880, edition 2.0, 2006, software for I&C systems performing
        category A functions. Copyrighted; cited by designation and edition
        only.
-   X11 IEC 61513, edition 2.0, 2011, nuclear power plant I&C important to
        safety. Copyrighted; cited by designation and edition only.
-   X12 IEC 62138, edition 2.0, 2018, software for I&C systems performing
        category B or C functions. Copyrighted; cited by designation and
        edition only.
-   X13 IAEA safety guides on computer-based safety systems of nuclear power
        plants (for example SSG-39). Copyrighted; cited by designation only.
-   X14 Regulatory Guide 1.152, Revision 4, July 2023 (ML23054A463), guidance
        on programmable logic controllers in non-safety applications. A US
        Government work and therefore public domain, but outside this pack's
        pinned source set; named as an adjacent document only.
-   X15 NUREG-0800 Branch Technical Position 7-18, Revision 6 (ML16019A327),
        and Branch Technical Position 7-19, Revision 9, May 2024
        (ML24005A077), with Standard Review Plan Appendix 7.1-D, Revision 1
        (ML16019A114), on guidance for evaluation of defense in depth and
        diversity. US Government works outside the pinned source set; named as
        adjacent documents only.
-   X16 NUREG/CR contractor reports supporting the endorsed standards (for
        example NUREG/CR-6463 on safety software). Named by designation only;
        no contractor-report text is reproduced.

Buy copyrighted items from IEEE, IEC, or IAEA as applicable. The designation
and edition citations above exist so a reader can locate the standards; the
cleared status of S1 to S7 and the exclusion rationale are recorded in
../../docs/SOURCE-VETTING.md.
